    {
      "bbox": [
        478,
        1154,
        1959,
        1910
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "I have learned from representatives of the New York Telephone Company of instances where city departments have announced a special telephone number where the public can call for information without making the proper arrangements for sufficient lines to handle the number of calls. As a result callers are inconvenienced by repeated busy signals and call the Mayor's Office to complain that they have been given a number to call but can't get through.",
